\pard\nowidctlpar\fs24\par
\cf2 2. <required parameters>\par
\cf6 Immediately after \cf1 <function parameter>\cf6 , there are generally 1 ~ 2 <required parameters>, indicating the objects of operation, such as files, directories, volume numbers, etc. In the [image volume number|image volume name] parameter, it is recommended to use the \cf2 image volume number\cf6 .\par
3. [Optional parameters]\par
[Optional parameter] At the end of WimTool command line, it is optional to indicate other functions performed by WimTool.\cf2\par
\par
\b V. Parameter description \b0\par
 \cf6 1. Mount the image\par
 (1). Read-only mount\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Mount\cf6   \cf8 <image file[,image volume number|image volume name]>  <target path>\cf6\par
Note: The image volume number or image volume name is only one of them, and the image file and the image volume number (or image volume name) are combined into a necessary parameter, using "connection; if the file directory name has spaces, it must be surrounded by".\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Mount\cf6   \cf8 "F:\\My Tools.WIM,2"  R:\\Toolbox\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  (2). Writeable mount\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /MountRW\cf6   \cf2 <image file[,image volume number|image volume name]>  <target path>\cf6\par
Note: The image volume number or image volume name is only one of them, and the image file and the image volume number (or image volume name) are combined into a necessary parameter, using "connection; if the file directory name has spaces, it must be surrounded by".\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /MountRW\cf6   \cf2 "F:\\My Tools.WIM,2"  R:\\Toolbox\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  (3). Reload\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ReMount\cf6   [target path]\par
Description: Remounting is to remount the specified "defective mount" and remount all "default mount" when omitting [target path].\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ReMount\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  2. Uninstall the image \par
 (1). Uninstall the specified image\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /UnMount\cf6   \cf2 <Tject Path|/All>\cf6   [/Commit|/Update]\par
Description: When <target path> is "/All", it means that all mount images are read-only uninstalled; "/Commit" means an image that can be uninstalled on the mount directory; and "/Update" means asking whether the specified directory can be unwrote.\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /UnMount\cf6   \cf2 R:\\Toolbox\cf6   /Commit\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /UnMount\cf6   \cf2 R:\\Toolbox\cf6\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /UnMount\cf6   /All \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  (2). Clear invalid mount\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /CleanUp\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  3. Untie the image \par
 (1). Silent, no progress in processing\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Apply\cf6   \cf2 <Image File[,Image Volume Number|Image Volume Name]>\cf6   \cf2 <Target Path|>\cf6   [Security Permission] [Decompression Rules] \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  (2). Window method, providing processing progress\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrFile\cf6   \cf2 <Image File[,Image Volume Number|Image Volume Name]>  <Tategoal Path>\cf6   [Security Permission] [Decompression Rules]\par
Description: [Security Permissions] Is "/NotAcl" And [decompression Rule] Is "/Config <configuration Profile>"\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Apply\cf6   \cf2 D:\\Test.WIM,2  D:\\PROGRAMS\cf6\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrFile\cf6   \cf2 D:\\Test.WIM,1  D:\\PROGRAMS  \cf6 /NotAcl\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrFile\cf6   \cf2 F:\\SysBack.WIM,2  C:\\\cf6   /NotAcl  /Config Config.INI \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  4. Make images \par
 (1). Silent, no progress in processing\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Capture\cf6   \cf2 <target path>  <image file[,image name]>\cf6   [compression type]  [startup marker]  [capture rule]\par
Description: [compression type] is "/Compress None|Xpress|Lzx|Lzms", [bootup tag] is "/Boot", [capture rule] is "/Config <configuration file>"\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Capture\cf6   \cf2 D:\\PROGRAMS  "D:\\Test.WIM,My Programs"\cf6   /Compress Xpress  /Boot \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  (2). Window method, provides processing progress and supports file filtering.\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi420 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /CompPath\cf6   \cf2 <Target Path|>  <image File[,Image Name]>\cf6   [Compression Type] [Start Marker] [Capture Rules]\par
Description: [compression type] is "/Compress None|Xpress|Lzx|Lzms", [bootup tag] is "/Boot", [capture rule] is "/Config <configuration file>"\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  /\cf1 CompPath\cf6   \cf2 D:\\WinPE  R:\\WinPE.WIM\cf6   /Boot\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /CompPath\cf6   \cf2 C:\\  F:\\SysBack.WIM\cf6   /Config Config.INI \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  5. Additional image(s)\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi315 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Append\cf6   \cf2 <target path>  <image file[,image name]>\cf6   [compression type] [startup tag] [capture rule]\par
Description: The [boot tag] is "/Boot" and the [capture rule] is "/Config <profile>"\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Append\cf6   \cf2 D:\\PROGRAMS  "D:\\Test.WIM,My Programs"\cf6   /Compress  Lzx  /Boot \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  6. Export and merge\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi315 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Export\cf6   <Imaging File[,Image Volume Number|Image Volume Name]>  <Imaging File>  [Compression Type]\par
Description: [Compression type] is "/Compression". When the compression type is "Lzms", it is executed in a window mode and provides processing progress and a cancel button\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Export\cf6   \cf2 F:\\SysBack.WIM,0  D:\\Test.WIM\cf6   /Compress Lzx \par

\pard\nowidctlpar  7. Split image\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi315 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Split\cf6   \cf2 <image file>  <image file,subcontract size>\cf6\par
Description: The subcontract size is in MB, which \cf2 is a required parameter\cf6 . \par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Split\cf6   \cf2 F:\\Test.WIM  R:\\SSS.WIM,100\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  8. Registration function\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi315 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Register\cf6   [/WimTemp TemporaryWorkingDirectory] [/MountPath BaseMountDirectory] [Icon] [Memu] [Exec]\par
Description: [Icon] [Memu] [Exec] Respectively represent Icon expansion, Menu expansion and File association.\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Register\cf6  Icon Memu  Exec  /WimTemp  F:\\WimTemp  /MountPath  F:\\MountPath.\par

\pard\nowidctlpar  9. Uninstall function\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\fi315 Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Unload\cf6   [Icon] [Memu] [Exec]\par
Description: Omitting optional parameters means registering all functions. \par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /Unload\cf6\par

\pard\nowidctlpar 10. Editing function\par
(1). Extract the file directory\par
Format: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrPath\cf6   \cf2 <image file[,image volume number|image volume name]>\cf6   <file directory within image|@[\\]file directory list file>  <target directory>\par
Note: Only one of the image volume number or image volume name is selected, and the image file and image volume number (or image volume name) are combined as a required parameter, and they are connected by ","; If there are spaces in the file directory name, it must be surrounded by "".\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrPath\cf6   \cf2 d:\\install.esd,2\cf6   windows\\system32\\wimgapi.dll  d:\\test.\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrPath\cf6   \cf2 d:\\install.esd,2\cf6   windows\\system32\\WIM*. *  d:\\test  //supports wildcards "? "and" * "\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrPath\cf6   \cf2 d:\\install.esd,2\cf6   @e:\\filelist.txt  d:\\test  //prefix "@" means that the file directory to be extracted is listed in e:\\filelist.txt.\par
Example: WimTool.EXE  \cf1 /ExtrPath\cf6   \cf2 d:\\install.esd,2\cf6   @\\FileList.TXT  d:\\test   //prefix "\\" means that the absolute path of FileList.TXT is omitted, which means that filelist.txt is in the same directory as the image.\par
