(4). The window operation method\par
On page 5 of WimTool, you can browse the volume image and file directory of WIM in addition to the file directory on the hard disk, and you can perform four operations such as \cf1 [extract], [append], [delete] and [rename]\cf6  on the volume image and file directory of WIM.\par
These four operations can be realized through the right mouse button menu; [Extract] and [Append] can be achieved by dragging with the mouse; [Rename] operation can also be realized by the shortcut key F2. [Extract], [Delete] and [Append] in the window can be operated in batches.\par
In the browse file directory window, you can return to the previous directory in turn by clicking the first item in the list "Previous directory" or the return icon at the lower left; Click the "serial number" in the header to directly return to the root directory of the system "My Computer".\par
\par
