\pard\nowidctlpar\ri1260\qj\cf2\b VI. Attention to use\b0\par
\cf6 1. WimTool must \cf1 run as an administrator\cf6 , and WimTool components must be installed correctly in the system to use all the functions of wimtool.\par
2. Some functions may not be available in the simplified WinPE system.\par
3. \cf1 The temporary directory of the system must have enough space\cf6 ; When used in PE, the temporary directory is recommended to be set on the hard disk.\par
4. Only one volume in an image has the startup mark; The volume number in the image is unique, while the volume name and volume description are only descriptions of the image volume, but they are not unique.\par
That is to say, different volumes in an image can have the same name and description.\par
5. When there is an error or abnormality in WIM file association in the system, please click [Cancel File Association] and then click [Set File Association] to repair it.\par
6. If you are not familiar with the configuration file of the captured image, please don't modify it, just use the default settings.\par
7. After switching languages, the main module interface of WimTool can take effect immediately, and the right-click menu needs to be restarted or logged out before it can take effect.\par
8. WimTool has the function of filtering and excluding files when capturing or decompressing images, and supports the file directory with wildcards. And' *', to understand the writing of filtering and exclusion rules, please see the INI file in the Languages directory.\par
Or click the [Profile] button on page 1 and click the [Default] button in the pop-up window;\par
9. WimTool uses the built-in configuration file by default when capturing or decompressing images. WinPE downloaded from the Internet may have special files in the Temp directory, and unpacking with WimTool may not start. Please know the built-in configuration file of WimTool.\par
